{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc","id":717559,"title":"Kindred and the CDC","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T23:29:50-07:00","id":717559,"title":"Kindred and the CDC","content":"I've mentioned before that I'm brewing up a VtR game set in Atlanta. Most of the pieces are in place for the city's infrastructure, and without any character sheets on my plate yet I'm mostly just spinning my wheels and filling in the gaps in the setting.<br /> <br /> One of my earliest hooks was that a sect of the Ordo Dracul are deeply entrenched in the campus of Emory University. It's a medical school, obvious fit in the first place, and there's the even more tantalizing promise of the Center For Disease Control right there, the seat of medical research with tunnels rumored to stretch across to other CDC campus and the city's major hospitals. That said, the nature of the beast means it's going to be heavily guarded. My original idea was to have a kindred embedded down there in some quarantined lab, but that seems simply not feasible given the level of security in the place. What's more likely is that there's some high ranking Dragon who's ghouled some doctors with clearance into the place. Mad science abounds and all that. Were she so inclined, she could visit a plague upon the city and all that jazz. It's unlikely to be a part of town the players would visit any time soon nor be a plot thread they'll pull in the near future, but the thought of a heist on one of the nation's most secure research laboratories is a tantalizing one. I could use some inspiration though. I might not draw on it, but it would be fun to hear about.<br /> <br /> What would you guys do if you had a juicy prospect like the CDC planted square in the middle of your setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:13:51-07:00","id":718060,"title":"","content":"I think one of the doctors being blood bonded would make for a pretty good hook for getting to stuff in the CDC, but it's a placed hardened against the influence of terrorists and spies and such, so I'd be very careful about how much you allow the Kindred to get close to that. In fact, there might be people like Task Force Valkyrie who guard the facility, possibly because of experiments in some other section that might be extra sensitive.<br /> <br /> An example of something they could have in those labs: Cymothoa Sanguinaria, from Night Horrors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 10-23-2015, 04:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T02:28:58-07:00","id":718290,"title":"","content":"One of the problems with ghouling the doctors is that they have their blood tested pretty regularly. Dominate might be a better course of action.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T03:44:47-07:00","id":718494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718290#post718290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems with ghouling the doctors is that they have their blood tested pretty regularly. Dominate might be a better course of action.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ghouls get isn't evident in your regular old blood as far as we know, I don't think, so I'm not sure if that's an issue?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T04:02:20-07:00","id":718550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718494#post718494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ghouls get isn't evident in your regular old blood as far as we know, I don't think, so I'm not sure if that's an issue?</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen anything indicating vampires no longer serve as a vector for contagious blood diseases. (If anything the implication is that it's even stronger in 2nd edition.) And CDC testing isn't regular because they don't want their employees carrying whatever diseases they're working with out into the unsuspecting public for many reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T04:47:49-07:00","id":718637,"title":"","content":"I can't see any reason why the presence of vitae in a ghoul's blood <i>wouldn't</i> be detected by a blood test.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T04:53:47-07:00","id":718640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Resplendent Fire</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718637#post718637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't see any reason why the presence of vitae in a ghoul's blood <i>wouldn't</i> be detected by a blood test.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vitae is the mystical power of the vampire mixed in his blood . After the blood is ingested by the ghoul, the power is dispersed in his body until is used. An analysis wouldn't reveal anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","user":"Raistlin","date":". 10-23-2015, 07:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T05:49:38-07:00","id":718709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Raistlin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718640#post718640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The vitae is the mystical power of the vampire mixed in his blood . After the blood is ingested by the ghoul, the power is dispersed in his body until is used. An analysis wouldn't reveal anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>A toxicology test can reveal that the individual ingested something that contained blood. It can even ascertain what time said blood was ingested. Under examination, vitae shows up as a strange combination of different types of blood that had been recently ingested by the vampire who produced the vitae sample examined.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:08:08-07:00","id":718736,"title":"","content":"Ah, Raistlin is correct about it not being in the blood. My mistake.<br /> <br /> I would still be extremely wary of making CDC types into ghouls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T06:51:25-07:00","id":718833,"title":"","content":"Actually, I'll even go one step further. A ghoul swallows the blood, it goes into his stomache. While the vitae, the mystical life energy, disperses throughout the ghoul's body, the actual swallowed blood remains in the digestive track, and leaves the body just like regular food. So, there's no reason for it to show up in a blood test, when its not even being absorbed into the circulatory system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:15:36-07:00","id":718908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718060#post718060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the doctors being blood bonded would make for a pretty good hook for getting to stuff in the CDC, but it's a placed hardened against the influence of terrorists and spies and such, so I'd be very careful about how much you allow the Kindred to get close to that. In fact, there might be people like Task Force Valkyrie who guard the facility, possibly because of experiments in some other section that might be extra sensitive.<br /> <br /> An example of something they could have in those labs: Cymothoa Sanguinaria, from Night Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, the CDC wouldn't have to have outside guards be Valkyrie- Valkyrie is a multi-agency task force, so there's no reason to believe that there aren't Valkyrie hunters who are CDC, especially since supernatural diseases are a thing. <br /> <br /> Other things the CDC might have in their labs- a strain of zombie disease or two from Antagonists, zoomorphic diseases from Skinchangers, infectious forms of lycanthropy and/or vampirism from hunter, the fountain of youth/living vampire bacteria from Wicked Dead, the abyssal parasites from Intruders, and possibly that STD from the werewolf night horrors book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T07:45:11-07:00","id":719141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc#post717559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would you guys do if you had a juicy prospect like the CDC planted square in the middle of your setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably have a vampire who lives down there, Obfuscated almost all the time. Probably a Morotrophian who gives lip service to the Invictus of the city but is actually a member of the Prima Invicta and occasionally makes withdrawals on their behalf when they need to wipe out or put a large population in danger. Otherwise he's fairly responsible and sees the workers as his herd and appreciates the importance of the place.<br /> <br /> A small coterie of Morbus would arrive, attempting to spread a strange disease in order to lure members of the CDC into action so they can study them in order to prepare for their larger plan, which likely involves a more dangerous outbreak. Maybe tie it into the Plague Angel himself, or his childer. I'd also tie in the Fire Touched werewolves of the Pure, taking over a nearby church or opening a new one to incorporate it on their grounds, exploring things tentatively but carefully, as the place would have a lot of spirits that wouldn't like them and they'd quickly realize there was something else guarding the place, if they didn't know exactly what. in the meantime they'd try to use their influence to bring other Pure packs in the area aligned towards them, or wipe out or convert Forsaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T08:01:49-07:00","id":719207,"title":"","content":"I've said it before, but the Trauma Center games for the Nintendo DS and Wii are perfect as inspiration for a Valkyrie CDC game. the advanced medical technology in the series would make an excellent addition to advanced armory for CDC hunters.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-23-2015, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:03:00-07:00","id":719481,"title":"","content":"What is your take on Atlanta's history?<br /> I been trying deal with whether strix would drawn to the battle for Atlanta and would some be destroyed in the burning.<br /> Was Sherman's March in part an attempt to deal with strix?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:37:09-07:00","id":719650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718550#post718550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't seen anything indicating vampires no longer serve as a vector for contagious blood diseases. (If anything the implication is that it's even stronger in 2nd edition.) And CDC testing isn't regular because they don't want their employees carrying whatever diseases they're working with out into the unsuspecting public for many reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>A blood born disease probably wouldn't survive very long in a vampire's blood, since their circulatory system doesn't function if they're not using the blush of life. Now, if the vampire contracted a disease from one vessel while under the effects of the blush, there would be a brief window when they could potentially pass it to a second vessel, if they were to feed again before the blush wore off. But after that the virus would probably die shortly after the vampires blood went cold.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T09:38:34-07:00","id":719655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=718060#post718060\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An example of something they could have in those labs: Cymothoa Sanguinaria, from Night Horrors.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bDo not want. Seriously, that section of Night Horrors has creeped me out more than anything else.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:01:54-07:00","id":719729,"title":"","content":"There's a bunch of great ideas here, guys. I'll sort through them shortly, but I think I've got a lot of material to draw from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719481#post719481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your take on Atlanta's history?<br /> I been trying deal with whether strix would drawn to the battle for Atlanta and would some be destroyed in the burning.<br /> Was Sherman's March in part an attempt to deal with strix?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy, don't get me started. Are you planning on running an Atlanta game? because my history and setting has gotten EXTENSIVE, probably in large part due to the fact that I've lived here my entire life. It's gotten ridiculous enough that I've considered formatting the bits and pieces out as a fan-made setting supplement, though I'm not sure if there'd be any interest in that.<br /> <br /> The details of Sherman's March is still foggy. It was either an unfortunate tragedy or an ambitious power move by an upstart kindred who would become Prince. Real estate, and particularly the unique real estate practices of segregation in Atlanta are one of the largest factors in the history and current power infrastructure of Atlanta. The throughline of modern power is a Prince who's rise to power dates back to Reconstruction (though he's currently in torpor while his childe leads), who has solidified his control by manipulating the value, both for mortals and immortals, of neighborhood housing markets. There was another big fire in 1917, not as extensive as Sherman's March, but targeting O4W, which was a predominantly black neighborhood at the time. There are rumors that both big fires were risky manipulations by this Prince, but there's a darker implication that a Strix is responsible, and that another such incident might be looming on the horizon. I'm leaving it ambiguous at the moment though to give me more flexibility as the game proceeds.<br /> <br /> Chances are, though, I'll probably be leaving Sherman's March as simply the result of wartime actions. I tend to lean more towards the philosophy that the lives (or unlives) of supernaturals are shaped by historical events rather than the other way around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-23-2015, 01:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:04:58-07:00","id":719736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719650#post719650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A blood born disease probably wouldn't survive very long in a vampire's blood, since their circulatory system doesn't function if they're not using the blush of life. Now, if the vampire contracted a disease from one vessel while under the effects of the blush, there would be a brief window when they could potentially pass it to a second vessel, if they were to feed again before the blush wore off. But after that the virus would probably die shortly after the vampires blood went cold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be a hell of an environment to accidentally create a low-temperature or necrophage bacterium, it occurs to me. Vitae tends to take care of itself, so it would probably be harmless to them, but could be either a reliable marker for kindred blood, or worse, communicable.<br /> <br /> Sorry. Spitballing disease ideas. Which sounds more gross in writing than it did in my head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:07:15-07:00","id":719741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719481#post719481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is your take on Atlanta's history?</div> </div> </div> </div>The <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Chicken\" target=\"_blank\">big chicken</a> was built by an insane Acolyte to ward off the strix, weirdly enough it seems to be working.<br /> <br /> The part of Underground Atlanta that isn't open to the public is the necropolis of the Nosferatu<br /> <br /> The Invictus once briefly took over Coke a Cola in the 80s and put vitae in New Coke, which explains why people liked it in the taste tests. they weren't expecting the backlash and peer pressure resulting from people's emotional attachment to the old formula to over come the blood bonds and the marketing campaign. They're doing it again with the re-release of SURGE, this time taking emotainal attachment into account.<br /> <br /> As for Sherman and the burning of Atlanta, the local vampires think that was about them and the strix, but it was actually about destroying the warehouses full of confederate super-weapons that were in Atlanta, the fire may not have got all the superweapons though...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 10-23-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:14:23-07:00","id":719752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719141#post719141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd probably have a vampire who lives down there, Obfuscated almost all the time. Probably a Morotrophian who gives lip service to the Invictus of the city but is actually a member of the Prima Invicta and occasionally makes withdrawals on their behalf when they need to wipe out or put a large population in danger. Otherwise he's fairly responsible and sees the workers as his herd and appreciates the importance of the place.<br /> <br /> A small coterie of Morbus would arrive, attempting to spread a strange disease in order to lure members of the CDC into action so they can study them in order to prepare for their larger plan, which likely involves a more dangerous outbreak. Maybe tie it into the Plague Angel himself, or his childer. I'd also tie in the Fire Touched werewolves of the Pure, taking over a nearby church or opening a new one to incorporate it on their grounds, exploring things tentatively but carefully, as the place would have a lot of spirits that wouldn't like them and they'd quickly realize there was something else guarding the place, if they didn't know exactly what. in the meantime they'd try to use their influence to bring other Pure packs in the area aligned towards them, or wipe out or convert Forsaken.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've strongly considered the idea of a vampire down there, either in the tunnels beneath or in some blocked off lab that's long forgotten, though I'd probably make them a Dragon. They've been embedded in the space as long as anyone can remember, communicating rarely with the rest of their chapter via cryptic messages sent, via Dominate, through facility workers. But the messages are becoming increasingly erratic and disturbing, and his compatriots on the outside are beginning to get worried. In my setting it would be a careful balance to walk for them. The Dragons rule the area pretty much unfettered by the Invictus Prince, who's seat of power is incredibly localized. The Dragons would have to weigh the threat of an outbreak or attack vs. asking for Invictus help, knowing the latter would weaken their own power and probably be used as pretext by ambitious Invictus to seize domain as their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:20:47-07:00","id":719764,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, I wasn't talking about Vitae NOT being a good vector for disease, I was just saying that if the CDC did blood tests on ghouls, I don't think they'd detect any anomalies from having consumed Vitae and become immortal. Maybe they'd seem unusually healthy? I don't think they'd be able to see what's going on though.<br /> <br /> On an entirely separate note, vampires ARE vectors for diseases in tainted blood, which is the root of stuff like plague hounds and the Morbus. Charlaquin provides a pretty good analysis of why this doesn't work if you get into the science of blood born diseases, but I have my suspicion that Kindred that become carriers aren't doing so thanks to science. Could be a fun thing to explore in the CDC homeland.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:24:07-07:00","id":719784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719764#post719764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, I wasn't talking about Vitae NOT being a good vector for disease, I was just saying that if the CDC did blood tests on ghouls, I don't think they'd detect any anomalies from having consumed Vitae and become immortal. Maybe they'd seem unusually healthy? I don't think they'd be able to see what's going on though.<br /> <br /> On an entirely separate note, vampires ARE vectors for diseases in tainted blood, which is the root of stuff like plague hounds and the Morbus. Charlaquin provides a pretty good analysis of why this doesn't work if you get into the science of blood born diseases, but I have my suspicion that Kindred that become carriers aren't doing so thanks to science. Could be a fun thing to explore in the CDC homeland.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I'm increasingly think that the threat of a blood-borne disease will become a major slow-burn plot in my chronicle, really highlight the disadvantage that comes from the more isolated fiefdoms that constitute Atlanta's kindred population and potentially establish the Strix as a menace that's been pulling the strings since forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:44:12-07:00","id":719837,"title":"","content":"Our last vampire game had a disease that was ravaging the vampire populace, created as a result of our last hunter game, where one of the characters wanted to wipe out vampires through a biological weapon. It didn't work but it killed more than a few elders and caused a lot of unrest once it went 'public' among the vampire communities, especially when neighboring domains warned them they'd bloodhunt any vampires they found leaving the infected territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719752#post719752\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've strongly considered the idea of a vampire down there, either in the tunnels beneath or in some blocked off lab that's long forgotten, though I'd probably make them a Dragon. They've been embedded in the space as long as anyone can remember, communicating rarely with the rest of their chapter via cryptic messages sent, via Dominate, through facility workers. But the messages are becoming increasingly erratic and disturbing, and his compatriots on the outside are beginning to get worried. In my setting it would be a careful balance to walk for them. The Dragons rule the area pretty much unfettered by the Invictus Prince, who's seat of power is incredibly localized. The Dragons would have to weigh the threat of an outbreak or attack vs. asking for Invictus help, knowing the latter would weaken their own power and probably be used as pretext by ambitious Invictus to seize domain as their own.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should go for it. Best result, the players are tagged to deal with it or otherwise have a say in what happens, affecting the political table of the entire territory. Worst result, it never comes up but afterwards you can let them know what was going on with the few hints they were provided about the Ordo getting antsy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-23-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T10:50:19-07:00","id":719868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719837#post719837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Our last vampire game had a disease that was ravaging the vampire populace, created as a result of our last hunter game, where one of the characters wanted to wipe out vampires. It didn't work but it killed more than a few elders and caused a lot of unrest once it went 'public' among the vampire communities, especially when neighboring domains warned them they'd bloodhunt any vampires they found leaving the infected territory.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You should go for it. Best result, the players are tagged to deal with it or otherwise have a say in what happens, affecting the political table of the entire territory. Worst result, it never comes up but afterwards you can let them know what was going on with the few hints they were provided about the Ordo getting antsy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't have more than basic sketches of some PCs yet, so I can't go full bore planning things, but I have a sketch of things in mind. The Invictus power structure is centralized in the downtown-midtown corridor. They control the heart of the city and the major transit routes in and out (They also host ambassadors from a couple of the major East coast cities. They've gotten paranoid after the Olympics brought in an infestation of Belial's Brood that threatened to rend the Masquerade). So the coterie will be out in the fringes of East Atlanta, taming the frontier to bring an Invictus presence to the rapidly gentrifying neighborhood. Still, they're not far from Decatur and the CDC. My thought is it will be more of a late game scenario. The coterie is brought in to deal with it. Failing or ignoring the issue brings in a catastrophic plague that devastates the Dragons and forces the Invictus into quarantine mode, further isolating their power and sending in their Hounds to clean up the infected in the area. It could upend the existing power structure and leave the players well positioned for some social climbing. So yeah, similar in a lot of ways to what you did, I suppose. Though it probably won't be explicitly designed to kill vampires. I still haven't settled on the specifics yet, but I figure a disease explicitly designed to spread with the feeding patterns of the kindred and risk the Masquerade on a sweeping level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 10-23-2015, 02:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T12:01:38-07:00","id":720050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kerensky</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719655#post719655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bDo not want. Seriously, that section of Night Horrors has creeped me out more than anything else.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the CS creeped the jeebus out of me.<br /> And then I discovered (and played) <i>The Last Of Us</i><b><i> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></i></b><br /> <a href=\"https://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media/image/upload/s--1_qyZCrS--/c_fill,fl_progressive,g_north,h_358,q_80,w_636/18ryrabz3rxqjjpg.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://i.kinja-img.com/gawker-media...bz3rxqjjpg.jpg</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2411-raistlin","name":"Raistlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"713"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T20:38:41-07:00","id":725016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/717559-kindred-and-the-cdc?p=719729#post719729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a bunch of great ideas here, guys. I'll sort through them shortly, but I think I've got a lot of material to draw from.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh boy, don't get me started. Are you planning on running an Atlanta game? because my history and setting has gotten EXTENSIVE, probably in large part due to the fact that I've lived here my entire life. It's gotten ridiculous enough that I've considered formatting the bits and pieces out as a fan-made setting supplement, though I'm not sure if there'd be any interest in that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I live in Chattanooga. The two cities have some intertwining connections all thru history.<br /> The battle for wauhatchie and the Battle above the clouds was a prelude to battle for Atlanta.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wauhatchie\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Battle_of_Wauhatchie_map.jpg/1280px-Battle_of_Wauhatchie_map.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wauhatchie\" target=\"_blank\"> Battle of Wauhatchie - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wauhatchie\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Wauhatchie </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}